OrionLayer open fix 134 — an injected RIGHT click is read by the call that drained it
=====================================================================================

Work order 443 (the engine commit's message says 444). orion2re on the branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.2 merged in), after
open fix 133. In src/ext/ext_api.cpp, src/ext/ext_api.h, src/game/platform.cpp
and src/game/platform.h; all of it inside `#ifdef ORION2RE_EXT`.

With the engine window SHOWN, a MSG_INJECT_RIGHT_CLICK was lost 3 times in 600
(measured on the build without this change, colonies button of the galaxy map,
help popup as the proof of effect; a fourth in a pair series: 4 of about 800).
It took the SDL path exactly as the left click did before open fix 130: an SDL
mouse-down and mouse-up pushed by ProcessInput, turned into queue events by the
SDL thread later, open to the game's own Clear_Fields_Above() queue pump.

The change, the same as open fix 130 for the other button. An
INJECT_RIGHT_CLICK drained inside fields::Get_Input's own Tick
(ext::g_click_direct_ok), not in a film, and only if no direct click was taken
in this Tick yet (ONE flag for both buttons: one direct click per Tick) calls
platform::Inject_Game_Right_Click, which enqueues the DOWN (mouse_buttons 2)
and the UP (0) from the game thread and sets the present pointer position; the
same Get_Input reads it. Every other Tick, a film and a second click in one
drain take the SDL path as before. The hold of open fix 129 is taken first, as
before. MSG_CANCEL_FIELD is not changed.

Live proof: see doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md entry 134 (Xvfb, no window manager,
no real pointer motion).

